egulated by protein kinase C phosphorylation in nerve terminals. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>365</volume>:<fpage>163</fpage>&#x02013;166.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8371759</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Rothstein, R. <year>1991</year>. Targeting, disruption, replacement, and allele rescue: integrative DNA transformation in yeast. <source>Meth. Enzymol.</source> <volume>194</volume>:<fpage>281</fpage>&#x02013;301.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2005793</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Sherman, F. <year>1991</year>. Getting started with yeast. <source>Meth. Enzymol.</source> <volume>194</volume>:<fpage>3</fpage>&#x02013;21.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2005794</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Slepnev, V.I., G.-C. Ochoa, M.H. Butler, D. Grabs, and P. De Camilli. <year>1998</year>. Role of phosphorylation in regulation of the assembly of endocytic coat complexes. <source>Science.</source> <volume>281</volume>:<fpage>821</fpage>&#x02013;824.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9694653</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Sun, Y., R. Taniguchi, D. Tanoue, T. Yamaji, H. Takematsu, K. Mori, T. Fujita, T. Kawasaki, and Y. Kozutsumi. <year>2000</year>. Sli2 (Ypk1), a homologue of mammalian protein kinase SGK, is a downstream kinase in the sphingolipid-mediated signaling pathway of yeast. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>20</volume>:<fpage>4411</fpage>&#x02013;4419.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10825204</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Tan, P.K., J.P. Howard, and G.S. Payne. <year>1996</year>. The sequence NPFXD defines a new class of endocytosis signal in <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>135</volume>:<fpage>1789</fpage>&#x02013;1800.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8991091</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Terrell, J., S. Shih, R. Dunn, and L. Hicke. <year>1998</year>. A function for monoubiquitination in the internalization of a G protein-coupled receptor. <source>Mol. Cell.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>193</fpage>&#x02013;202.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9659916</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Wilde, A., E.C. Beattie, L. Lem, D.A. Riethof, S.H. Liu, W.C. Mobley, P. Soriano, and F.M. Brodsky. <year>1999</year>. EGF receptor signaling stimulates SRC kinase phosphorylation of clathrin, influencing clathrin redistribution and EGF uptake. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>96</volume>:<fpage>677</fpage>&#x02013;687.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10089883</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Zanolari, B., S. Friant, K. Funato, C. Sutterlin, B.J. Stevenson, and H. Riezman. <year>2000</year>. Sphingoid base synthesis requirement for endocytosis in <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic>. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>2824</fpage>&#x02013;2833.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10856228</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Zha, X., L.M. Pierini, P.L. Leopold, P.J. Skiba, I. Tabas, and F.R. Maxfield. <year>1998</year>. Sphingomyelinase treatment induces ATP-independent endocytosis. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>140</volume>:<fpage>39</fpage>&#x02013;47.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9425152</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn1"><label>*</label><p>Abbreviations used in this paper: DIC, differential interference contrast&#x0003b; HA, hemagglutinin&#x0003b; LY, Lucifer yellow.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>